course: dictionary
lesson: 5682
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word lobster can name a sea animal, a food, or a way of describing someone with a bad sunburn. You do not need to guess. Read the words around it and ask which meaning fits.
explain: «They went with the lobsters to the dance, got thrown out to sea, and fell a long way.» Lobsters here are animals, because things that are thrown out to sea and fall are living creatures, not food. The meaning is a sea animal.
explain: «Toad hunts out cold chicken, trifle and lobster salad.» Chicken, trifle and salad are all foods, so lobster must mean the meat we eat. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A lobster is a sea animal with a hard shell, ten legs and two big claws.
fact: Lobsters are related to crabs, and they have an outer skeleton called an exoskeleton.
fact: Lobster can also mean the meat of the animal, eaten as an expensive seafood.
fact: A live lobster is usually dark greenish brown or bluish, and it turns red only when it is cooked.
fact: Lobsters have no backbone, so they are invertebrates.
exercise: «The lobster had ten legs and two big claws.» What is a lobster? | A bright red hat | A small fish with fins | *A sea animal with a hard shell | A kind of seaweed
exercise: Toad hunts out cold chicken, trifle and lobster salad. What does lobster mean here? | A trap for catching animals | A person who is badly sunburnt | *The meat of the animal, eaten as food | A kind of dance
exercise: Dad came home from the beach red as a lobster. What does this phrase mean? | Happy and dancing | Very cold and blue | Full of food | *Badly sunburnt
test: «The fishermen hauled up their lobster pot.» What is a lobster pot? | *A trap for catching lobsters | A kind of boat with sails | A pan for cooking dinner | A flower bed by the sea
test: «A live lobster is dark greenish brown; it turns red only when it is cooked.» Why does the lobster turn red? | It has too much sun | *It has been cooked | It is angry with the cook
exam: «Some of the strangest animals in the aquarium are not fish at all: jellyfish, octopuses, cuttlefish, sea stars and lobsters have no backbone.» In this sentence, what does lobsters mean? | *Sea animals with no backbone | A kind of dance | A cooked meal in a restaurant | A sunburnt person
